        "text": "According to Donald J. Ramsell (Respondent), according to Donald J. Ramsell (Respondent), according to Donald J. Ramsell (Respondent), the respondent argues that a mass, suspicionless seizure of innocent citizens without exigent circumstances violates the Fourth Amendment, citing Indianapolis v. Edmond as controlling precedent."
